description:
rnews_main.rs:193–196 and rnews_main.rs:267–270 contain identical 4-line blocks:

    let now_ms = std::time::SystemTime::now()
        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)
        .unwrap_or_default()
        .as_millis() as u64;

One occurrence seeds the HLC at startup; the other timestamps each accepted article. Both could call a one-liner helper, e.g.:

    fn wall_clock_ms() -> u64 {
        std::time::SystemTime::now()
            .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)
            .unwrap_or_default()
            .as_millis() as u64
    }

This is a minor mechanical issue but the duplication does mean a future change (e.g. using a monotonic source) must be made in two places.
